<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2010/07/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>Ardalis.MinimalClean.Template</id>
    <title>ASP.NET Minimal Clean Architecture Solution</title>
    <version>12.1.0</version>
    <authors>Steve Smith</authors>
    <description>
      A simplified Clean Architecture template using vertical slice architecture in a single project. 
      Perfect for MVPs, smaller applications, or teams wanting architectural guidance without multi-project complexity.
      Features Domain-Driven Design patterns, FastEndpoints, Entity Framework Core, and optional Aspire support.
      Built with .NET 11 and C#.
    </description>
    <language>en-US</language>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/ardalis/CleanArchitecture</projectUrl>
    <releaseNotes>
      12.1.0
      * Upgrade to Aspire 17. Running the Aspire app host (F5, dotnet run, or aspire run) now requires the Aspire CLI, which provides the orchestrator and dashboard. Building and running the Web project directly don't need it.
      * The app host no longer uses the obsolete Aspire.AppHost.Sdk. It references Aspire.Hosting.Dotnet and starts the Web project with AddDotnetProject instead of the obsolete AddProject&lt;TProject&gt;.
      * Update Scalar.AspNetCore to 3.0.2 and Serilog.AspNetCore to 11.0.0.
      * Remove a machine-specific local package source from nuget.config.
      * Security: migrations and seed data now run on startup only in Development, or when DatabaseOptions:ApplyMigrationsOnStartup is true, and a failed migration stops the app from starting instead of being logged and ignored.
      * Security: outside Development, unhandled exception messages are no longer returned to clients.
      * Security: the email sender requires STARTTLS by default and can authenticate with Mailserver:Username and Mailserver:Password. Development uses plain SMTP for the local Papercut server. The Mailserver:Server setting was ignored; it is now Mailserver:Hostname.
      * Security: each new solution gets its own UserSecretsId instead of sharing the template's.
      * See the v12.0 to v12.1 migration guide: https://cleanarchitecture.ardalis.com/migration-guides/v12-0-to-v12-1/

      12.0.1
      * No changes to the template. Released to keep the version in step with Ardalis.CleanArchitecture.Template 12.0.1.

      12.0.0
      * Version now matches Ardalis.CleanArchitecture.Template; both templates ship together (previously 1.1.1).
      * Upgrade to .NET 11 and the latest stable NuGet packages, including FastEndpoints 9.
      * Add NsDepCop rules that enforce dependency boundaries between feature slices at build time.
      * Fix file renames for project names that aren't valid namespaces.
      * New solutions no longer include the package icon (icon.png).
      * See the v11 to v12 migration guide: https://cleanarchitecture.ardalis.com/migration-guides/v11-to-v12/
    </releaseNotes>
    <packageTypes>
      <packageType name="Template" />
    </packageTypes>
    <tags>Web ASP.NET "Clean Architecture" "Vertical Slice" minimal ddd domain-driven-design clean-architecture ardalis FastEndpoints</tags>
    <icon>./content/icon.png</icon>
    <readme>README.md</readme>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="MinimalClean\**" target="content" exclude="**\bin\**;**\obj\**;**\.git\**;**\.vs\**;**\.vscode\**;**\*.user" />
    <file src="README.md" />
    <file src="icon.png" target="content" />
  </files>
</package>
